## Update v0.9.3 release notes and README after deployment validation

Context:
The 0.9.3 build was deployed to the `ontobricks-09x` instance and validated
live (app smoke, MCP smoke, scenario campaign). The release notes did not yet
cover the dependency security work, the lockfile URL fix, or the test-hygiene
and timestamp cleanups, and they did not record the live validation. The
README "What's new in 0.9.3" block also lacked the security floors. The Graph
Chat upgrade note claimed 8192 is a Foundation Model ceiling, which the code
does not establish; it now states the configured range only.

Changes:

1. releases/ReleaseNotes_V0.9.3.md
   Added live validation results to the test status header.
   Added a "Dependency security floors" highlight (Dependabot #318, #325–#329).
   Added a "Dependencies and maintenance" section (security floors, public
   lockfile URLs, pytest/pyproject warning filters, `utcnow` replacement).
   Reworded the Graph Chat `max_tokens` upgrade note to the accepted range.
   Added a dependency upgrade note (`databricks-sql-connector` ≥ 4.7.0, `make deploy`).
2. README.md
   Added a "Dependency security floors" bullet to the 0.9.3 "What's new" block.

Modified files:
- releases/ReleaseNotes_V0.9.3.md
- README.md
- changelogs/v0.9.3/benoitcayladbx_2026-11-21.log

Tests: documentation-only change; no code modified. Last full run before this
update: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` → 9712 passed, 337 skipped,
8 deselected. Live validation on `ontobricks-09x`: app smoke 11 passed, MCP
smoke 6 passed, scenario campaign 7 passed (validation 13 passed, 0 failed).
